msgid "`ToolServerConnection.auth_type: system_oauth` resolves the caller's token through `oauth_manager.get_oauth_token(user.id, oauth_session_id)` and presents it as the Bearer"
msgstr "`ToolServerConnection.auth_type: system_oauth` risolve il gettone del chiamante `oauth_manager.get_oauth_token(user.id, oauth_session_id)` e lo presenta come il Cuscinetto"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`Unit tests` verify isolated logic."
msgstr "`Unit tests` verificare la logica isolata."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`UsersLookup` yields the `no-reply` user dict used to derive `from` and `password`. Missing entries MUST yield an empty dict. The fallback for `from` is then `root@<inventory_hostname>.localdomain`."
msgstr "`UsersLookup` produce `no-reply` dict utilizzato per derivare `from` e `password`. Le voci scomparse devono cedere una ditta vuota. Il ritorno per `from` è allora `root@<inventory_hostname>.localdomain`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`Visual Studio Code <https://code.visualstudio.com/>`__ is a powerful source code editor with a wide plugin ecosystem, supporting development workflows across many languages and platforms. See also the `Arch Wiki - Development Tools <https://wiki.archlinux.org/title/Category:Development>`__ and general `Software Engineering <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Software_engineering>`__ on Wikipedia."
msgstr "`Visual Studio Code <https://code.visualstudio.com/>`__ è un potente editor di codici sorgente con un ampio ecosistema plugin, supportando i flussi di lavoro di sviluppo in molte lingue e piattaforme. Vedi anche `Arch Wiki - Development Tools <https://wiki.archlinux.org/title/Category:Development>`__ e generale `Software Engineering <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Software_engineering>`__ su Wikipedia."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`Visual Studio Code <https://github.com/microsoft/vscode>`__ in a selectable flavor: the distribution’s Code - OSS build, VSCodium, or Microsoft’s own binary."
msgstr "`Visual Studio Code <https://github.com/microsoft/vscode>`__ in un sapore selezionabile: la distribuzione Code - OSS costruire, VSCodium, o binario di Microsoft."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`WordPress <https://en.wordpress.org/>`__ is a versatile and widely used `content management system (CMS) <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Content_management_system>`__ that powers millions of websites, from blogs and portfolios to e-commerce and corporate sites. This deployment provides a containerized WordPress instance optimized for multisite operation, advanced media management, and extensive plugin support, allowing you to fully leverage the rich features of the WordPress software."
msgstr "`WordPress <https://en.wordpress.org/>`__ è un versatile e ampiamente usato `content management system (CMS) <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Content_management_system>`__ che alimenta milioni di siti web, da blog e portafogli a e-commerce e siti aziendali. Questa distribuzione fornisce un containerizzato WordPress istanza ottimizzata per il funzionamento multisito, gestione multimediale avanzata e ampio supporto plugin, che consente di sfruttare pienamente le caratteristiche ricche delle WordPress software."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`Zammad <https://zammad.org/>`__ is an open-source helpdesk and ticketing system. Agents handle customer requests across email, chat, phone and web; customers can open tickets from a self-service portal."
msgstr "`Zammad <https://zammad.org/>`__ è un sistema di helpdesk e ticketing open source. Gli agenti gestiscono le richieste dei clienti attraverso e-mail, chat, telefono e web; i clienti possono aprire i biglietti da un portale self-service."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`Zoom <https://zoom.us/>`__ is a popular video conferencing application for online meetings, webinars, and collaboration."
msgstr "`Zoom <https://zoom.us/>`__ è una popolare applicazione di videoconferenza per incontri online, webinar e collaborazione."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`[user@]host:/dev/...` → a device on the host, recovered over ssh then pulled; `[user@]host:/image` → the image is pulled and recovered locally (`device` / `full`)"
msgstr "`[user@]host:/dev/...` → un dispositivo sull'host, recuperato sopra ssh poi tirato; `[user@]host:/image` → l'immagine è tirato e recuperato localmente (`device` / `full`)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`_as_bool` MUST accept the usual string forms (`true|false|yes|no|1|0|on|off`), booleans, and numbers. Every boolean decision in the fallbacks MUST use it so that `SYSTEM_EMAIL_*` values coming from YAML, environment variables, or already-coerced facts all behave the same."
msgstr "`_as_bool` SOLO accettare le consuete forme di stringa (`true|false|yes|no|1|0|on|off`), booleani e numeri. Ogni decisione booleana nei fallback deve usarla in modo che `SYSTEM_EMAIL_*` valori provenienti da YAML, variabili di ambiente, o fatti già saldati tutti si comportano lo stesso."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`_compute` MUST delegate to three other lookup plugins rather than re-reading project state directly:"
msgstr "`_compute` DOVE delegare ad altri tre plugin di ricerca piuttosto che rileggere lo stato del progetto direttamente:"

